{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1337577-should-i-begin-with-mortals-or-gts","id":1337577,"title":"Should I Begin With Mortals or GTS???","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-23T19:48:40-07:00","id":1337577,"title":"Should I Begin With Mortals or GTS???","content":"So, it's been a long time since I've run any WOD, but it looks like that might be changing. However, some of my players are kind of new, and I really want to introduce them to the ghost rules of WOD. But time is something of an issue, and, well, should I try to do a mortal game first, or should I just drop them into GTS, and introduce the ghost rules through that? How good is GTS as an intro game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24164-marengo","name":"Marengo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-23T23:36:07-07:00","id":1337596,"title":"","content":"I often create a little &quot;tutorial&quot; as mortals for new players, it helps them to learn first the basic rules of the system, then you add the splat rules.<br /> I never played geist, but to me it seem less complex than other splats like mage, werewolf or demon, mostly because the mindset of a sineaters is not too different from the human perspective.<br /> For learning the ghost rules you could add a ghost NPC of a deceased relative that they start to see after the transformation, it could be a kind of mentor for them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-29T02:18:01-07:00","id":1338421,"title":"","content":"Maybe a very long and adventurous prelude in G:tSE should work well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-04T19:32:50-08:00","id":1365435,"title":"","content":"Run mortals for 2-3 session - and then 'kill' PCs, so they become Sin-Eaters. It's probably best way to run introductions for new players in <b>CoD</b> games, on general. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}